# Barre Shapes: E, Em, A and Am Shapes (repertoire plan: st-barre-shapes). An original 16-bar
# chord study: the four movable barre shapes, one bar each with four steady down-strums, then a
# five-bar progression that mixes them. Say the root aloud on beat 1 of every bar (the words under
# the strums): that is the note under finger 1 on string 6 (E and Em shapes) or string 5 (A and Am
# shapes), the string the root lives on.
#   E shape   (root on string 6): F 133211, G 355433, A 577655
#   Em shape  (root on string 6): Fm 133111, Gm 355333, Am 577555
#   A shape   (root on string 5): Bb x13331, B x24442, C x35553
#   Am shape  (root on string 5): Bm x24432, Cm x35543
#   Together: C (A shape, fret 3), Am (Em shape, fret 5), F (E shape, fret 1), G (E shape, fret 3), C.
title: Barre Shapes: E, Em, A and Am Shapes
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord study for Sixstring Academy
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: barre chords, movable shapes, root on string 6, root on string 5
tempo: 80
time: 4/4
key: C

